  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Humid with additional showers/thunderstorms expected\nthis early this morning with another round later this afternoon\nand evening and a 3rd round late tonight.\n\nVery busy night with significant, potentially life threatening \nflash flooding still ongoing across portions of Somerset Cty,\nmainly in the SW corner of the County, near Confluence where\nwater rescues were occurring and the Youghiogheny River rose\nabout 9 feet in just 2-3 hours.\n\nThis initial MCS that caused the flash flooding issues and \ntraining TSRA across the Laurel Highlands is racing to the east\nacross Central PA and storms will slowly weaken/dissipate as \nthey move east of the Susq Valley. \n\nDrier for the mid to late morning (very similar to Monday),\nfollowed by another round or two of strong to potentially SVR\nTSRA, likely concentrated over the southern two thirds of the\nstate. \n\nMost places in the CWA will see a few to several tenths of an\ninch of rain over the next 12 hours or so, with similar\nadditional amounts late tonight. Localized 1-2 inch amounts are\npossible where 2-3 TSRA train over the same locations\nconsidering PWAT values over 1.6 inches across southern PA.  \n\nA brief period of drier air pushes into the state for Wednesday,\nbut lingering PWATs over 1.4 inches across Southern PA and the\nclose proximity of a slowly swd moving cold front settling over\nthe virginias will keep the chc for showers and TSRA across our\nsouthern zones Wed into Thursday.  \n\n-----------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Much more comfortable humidity and slightly cooler\ntemps for Friday and Saturday.\n\nA push of relatively cooler and drier air accompanies \nseasonably strong/Canadian high pressure building southeast from\nthe Upper Midwest. GEFS PWAT anomalies dip to 1 sigma below\nnormal, or under 0.8 of an inch for later Friday and Saturday.",
